  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Takur Das vs State And Ors. on 14 November, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 632 of 1994 Revisionist :- Takur Das Opposite Party :- State And Ors. Counsel for Revisionist :- Sunil Kumar,Pradeep Kumar Bhardwaj Counsel for Opposite Party :- A.G.A. Hon'ble Sudhir Agarwal,J. 1.",
    "facts": "4. It is contended that there was no compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954. Court below found that Public Analyst report was sent by registered post which was received back without service. Thereafter, it was given to the revisionist in the Court itself after two years i.e. on 28.01.1988 and therefore, valuable right of revisionist under Section 13(2) of Act, 1954 is violated but Court below has said that after receipt of report, revisionist also submitted an application for re-testing, which was rejected by Trial Court and on that basis adverse inference has been drawn against revisionist. 5. It is submitted that compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954 is a necessary and mandatory requirement otherwise entire proceedings are vitiated.",
    "arguments": "6. The view taken by Courts below, I find, is in the teeth of judgment of Supreme Court in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019 and in para 15 of judgment, Court has said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "6. The view taken by Courts below, I find, is in the teeth of judgment of Supreme Court in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019 and in para 15 of judgment, Court has said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report."
  },
